In cases where a provided layer matched the `layerName` to rollup to, this method was returning a "simplified view" for all provided layers, eg:
```
"article4": {
 value: true,
},
"article4.canterbury.hmo": {
  value: true,
}
```

Now, for rendering the PlanningConstraints component and easier debugging, we only simplify the "granular" variable entries and preserve all properties on the "parent" variable, eg:
```
"article4": {
  text: "is subject to Article 4 Restriction(s)",
  description: "BLACKFRIARS STREET 28,29,30, KING STREET 10 TO 15, MILL LANE 19,20",
  value: true,
  type: "warning",
  data: {
    OBJECTID: 72963,
    REF: "Article 4 Direction 1985",
    LOCATION_1: "BLACKFRIARS STREET 28,29,30, KING STREET 10 TO 15, MILL LANE 19,20",
    DESCRIPTIO: "Effective 29 November 1985"
  }
},
"article4.canterbury.hmo": {
  value: true
}
```

In the future, it may make sense to take this a step further and convert the parent `data` property into an array that can reflect _each_ of the intersecting feature properties (even though they may have different keys?), but I don't think that's necessary yet.  (& in theory, the Digital Land API will give us a clean list of all intersecting features with standardized properties)

